From 63ee443211da513e1f7f41c3629c861d6e0f6d0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 01:59:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Five spells and six weapons that ended the session when you
 used them

Three things were reported from play on 2026-09-21. One was already fixed
(the Barrows chest flush moved into a queue in 0c46760b). The other two were
the same bug wearing different clothes: CONTENT THAT EXISTS AND CANNOT BE
REACHED WITHOUT BEING LOGGED OUT.

Iban's staff had no crush_sound. All three of a staff's styles are crush, so
~combat_swing_anim_and_synth returned null and player_melee.rs2 handed
sound_synth a null on the first swing. Checking every weapon against the style
table its category actually resolves to - which is combat.rs2's switch, not the
category's name - found six: Iban's staff, the magic secateurs, the void knight
mace, the Tzhaar-ket-em and both castle wars banners. The Tzhaar-ket-em's params
all said slash_ while weapon_crush falls through to the unarmed row, so it had
neither sound nor animation. castlewars_maindoor.rs2 has carried an
`if (%com_attacksound ! null)` for this the whole time - the symptom patched
where it showed, not where it came from.

Iban Blast had no row in magic_spell_table, so ~get_spell_data hit its own
error() and took the connection with it. Writing the rule to catch that found
FOUR MORE in the same state: Crumble Undead, Saradomin Strike, Claws of Guthix
and Flames of Zamorak. Every one has a finished script - the Mage Arena gate,
the god cape and staff check, the 3/2 charged scaling, Guthix draining defence,
Zamorak draining magic - and nobody had ever successfully cast one. All five
rows are the wiki's numbers, read today, with the cache's own art.

Also: choosing an autocast spell now turns autocast ON. @open_autocast_interface
zeroes the bit before the picker opens and choosing a spell never set it again,
so the spell name appeared, the lamp stayed grey and the next click was a melee
swing - which is how "ibans staff autocasting fire wave" became a melee script
error.

Three new rs2check rules, all proven failable by the selftest: 19, a weapon
swung on a style it has no sound for; 21, a spell script asking for a row that
is not there; 22, a combat row missing anim or spotanim_target, the two fields
player_magic.rs2 reads with no guard. Plus combat_battery.py for the part a
linter cannot know - the numbers and the three-way autocast agreement between a
script, a varbit and an interface - and combat_mutate.py, 18 mutations, each
caught by its own check.

rs2check 0 ERROR 0 CHECK, selftest PASS on all 21 rules, twelve batteries ALL
PASS. NOT compiled: npm is still 403ing zod, so no Engine-TS clone would
install. CI's pack job is the build.

